<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::negotiation_intensity" target="global_inflation_bond_st::broad_currency_index" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained increase in substantive diplomatic negotiations reduces acute geopolitical risk premia and safe‑haven demand, causing the dominant safe‑haven currency's trade‑weighted index to weaken as capital reallocates to risk assets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_inflation_bond_st</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::negotiation_intensity" target="middle_east_ir_escalatio::diplomatic_engagement" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained, resource‑intensive diplomatic negotiations over the Russia–Ukraine conflict absorb political capital and diplomatic bandwidth, reducing the frequency and scale of formal and informal engagement available to manage or de‑escalate crises in the Middle East.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">middle_east_ir_escalatio</data>
</edge>
