  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising perceived risk of oil supply disruptions from Middle East escalation increases urgency among energy‑dependent states to engage diplomatically with Russia and other suppliers to secure flows or carve out exemptions, raising the frequency and depth of negotiations related to the Russia–Ukraine conflict and energy provision.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_ir_escalatio</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
