<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_restrict" target="global_inflation_bond_st::broad_currency_index" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Stricter export controls on advanced semiconductors reduce trade and investment flows to targeted foreign markets and trigger capital reallocation and safe‑haven demand into the issuer currency, mechanically appreciating the broad currency index.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_inflation_bond_st</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_restrict" target="middle_east_ir_escalatio::military_tension_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter export controls on advanced semiconductors push China to accelerate military-technical cooperation and transfers with regional partners (notably Iran) and to increase force posture in response to perceived containment, provoking higher US/regional readiness and confrontational deployments in the Middle East.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">middle_east_ir_escalatio</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_restrict" target="middle_east_ir_escalatio::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Newly restrictive export controls raise market uncertainty and a geopolitical risk premium—including expectations of retaliatory measures against shipping and trade—producing short-term upward pressure on oil prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">middle_east_ir_escalatio</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_restrict" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Broad, extra‑territorial US export controls force allied governments and firms to adopt divergent implementation and waiver policies (e.g., differing rules for chip exports and investment screening), producing disputes over trade and defense coordination that reduce policy alignment among states supporting Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_restrict" target="transatlantic_security_s::negotiation_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">New or tightened U.S. export controls on advanced semiconductors force allied capitals and exporters to seek rapid policy alignment, waivers and supply‑management agreements, driving an immediate increase in formal and ad hoc diplomatic negotiations.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">transatlantic_security_s</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_restrict" target="transatlantic_security_s::alliance_unity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Broad U.S. export restrictions create asymmetric economic costs for European and other partners (differing exposure of national industries), producing disagreements over implementation and carve‑outs that weaken coordinated coalition policy.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">transatlantic_security_s</data>
</edge>
