<edge source="transatlantic_security_s::alliance_unity" target="transatlantic_security_s::deterrence_credibility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="transatlantic_security_s::alliance_unity" target="transatlantic_security_s::escalation_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
</edge>
<edge source="transatlantic_security_s::alliance_unity" target="global_inflation_bond_st::ten_year_bond_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger allied cohesion increases coordinated military and fiscal backing (direct aid, guarantees, wartime spending), raising expected sovereign issuance and risk premia which push ten‑year yields higher.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">transatlantic_security_s</data>
  <data key="d40">global_inflation_bond_st</data>
</edge>
<edge source="transatlantic_security_s::alliance_unity" target="middle_east_ir_escalatio::military_tension_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger transatlantic alliance cohesion produces coordinated forward deployments, joint exercises and escort operations in proximate waters, which regional adversaries interpret as escalatory and respond with raised readiness and reciprocal military manoeuvres.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">transatlantic_security_s</data>
  <data key="d40">middle_east_ir_escalatio</data>
</edge>
<edge source="transatlantic_security_s::alliance_unity" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_coercion_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A more unified transatlantic alliance enables faster, larger and more predictable military assistance and coordinated deterrent postures that raise Moscow's expected costs of offensive operations, leading it to scale back kinetic coercion.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">transatlantic_security_s</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="transatlantic_security_s::alliance_unity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_restrict" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter policy coordination among transatlantic allies permits synchronized legal design and simultaneous implementation of broader, more restrictive semiconductor export controls targeting Chinese access to advanced nodes and equipment.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">transatlantic_security_s</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="transatlantic_security_s::alliance_unity" target="concept::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">instance_of</data>
</edge>
